0016: def main(grid: np.ndarray) -> np.ndarray:
0017:     """
0018:     Split the two-color object horizontally, swap its colors, and slide the upper half to the right.
0019: 
0020:     Input structure:
0021:     - The grid has one background color and exactly two foreground colors.
0022:     - All foreground pixels form one 4-connected object with an even-height bbox.
0023:     - The object has foreground pixels on both rows adjacent to its horizontal midpoint.
0024: 
0025:     Rule:
0026:     - Split the object into upper and lower halves at the midpoint of its bbox.
0027:     - Swap the two foreground colors in both halves.
0028:     - Keep the lower half in place and shift the upper half right until its lower-left
0029:       boundary pixel is diagonally adjacent to the lower half's upper-right boundary pixel.
0030: 
0031:     Key insight:
0032:     - The object is not copied or reflected; it is broken at the horizontal waist,
0033:       recolored by exchanging the two visible object colors, then rejoined diagonally.
0034:     """
